id: pm-context-3s5f
title: Raise pm-context source coverage to enforced 100/100/100/100
description: "Close every genuine source coverage gap in index.ts and context-usage.ts with fast behavior-driven tests, then make 100 percent statements, branches, functions, and lines an unskippable release gate. Current honest c8 baseline is 91.78/81.93/95.31/91.78."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: coverage,quality-gate,release-readiness,tdd
created_at: "2026-07-26T14:29:15.160Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-10T14:51:27.403Z"
assignee: codex
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "c8 reports 100 percent statements, branches, functions, and lines for all source modules; release:check enforces all four thresholds; integration tests use real throwaway pm trackers and the SDK host harness; mutation or equivalent anti-cheat evidence demonstrates assertions detect regressions; tests remain deterministic and fast"
severity: high
environment: pm-context 2026.7.26 on Node 22 plus TypeScript 7 and c8 12
repro_steps: Run NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null npx c8 --all --include=dist/index.js --include=dist/context-usage.js --reporter=text node --test dist-test/*.js and inspect the aggregate row
expected_result: All maintained source is behaviorally exercised and the release gate rejects any metric below 100 percent.
actual_result: "Baseline after the SDK context review fixes: 91.78 percent statements, 81.93 branches, 95.31 functions, and 91.78 lines; package.json does not yet enforce coverage thresholds."
affected_version: 2026.7.26
component: testing
customer_impact: Uncovered command and rendering branches can regress without blocking release.
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-10T14:39:18.310Z",codex-sol,"Complete-source quality work is linked to the existing context-usage implementation owner pm-context-ci6v. Retain this open quality owner and its assignment; no competing claim or replacement issue. Current baseline measures six of eleven authored executables natively; broad ten-source c8 records 3789/3837 statements and lines, 1158/1164 branches and 102/103 functions, with shell behavior separately unmeasured. The required target remains all authored source and gate/template code with independent statement measurement and no coverage exceptions."
  "2026-10-10T14:50:53.732Z",codex-sol,"Independent focused repair: LCOV invalidates before configuration parsing and on runner or inventory failure. Three real filesystem assertions fail with original source and pass after byte-identical restoration. Actual existing YAML verifier accepts real scalar and array dependency fixtures and rejects seven workflow or marker drifts. Full native suite now passes 301 tests with unchanged thresholds. Broader pre-repair c8 observation reached 3837/3837 statements and lines, 1177/1178 branches and 102/102 reported functions across ten TS/JS executables; one non-Error conversion branch, shell coverage and zero function counters for two operational scripts remain explicit. Whole AST presence inventory includes 247 callables (57 with JSDoc) and 809 declaration/type nodes (115 with JSDoc); these are presence counts, not high-quality documentation approval. Closed helper owner pm-context-qu0a remains held by codex; managed launcher callback remains undocumented under its byte-identical template contract. No source is excluded or renamed to claim whole-source completion."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T14:29:15.160Z",codex,Created separately from pm-context-lk82 so review correctness can ship without falsely claiming the mandated 100 percent coverage target is already met.
  "2026-07-26T15:10:43.852Z",codex,"Remeasured after final CodeRabbit remediation with c8 12 over both generated runtime modules: 91.78 statements,81.93 branches,95.31 functions,and 91.78 lines. The open 100/100/100/100 gap remains explicit and is not represented as complete."
